menu "MQTT"

    config NCLE_MQTT_ENABLE
        bool "Enable MQTT cloud connectivity"
        default n
        help
            Publish milk readings and receive commands over MQTT.
            When disabled, the firmware behaves identically to the
            non-MQTT build.

    config NCLE_MQTT_BROKER_URI
        string "MQTT broker URI"
        depends on NCLE_MQTT_ENABLE
        default "mqtt://broker.hivemq.com:1883"
        help
            Broker URI. Dev: mqtt://broker.hivemq.com:1883 (plain).
            Production later: mqtts://<server>:8883 (TLS) via a config change.

    config NCLE_MQTT_USERNAME
        string "MQTT username (empty = anonymous)"
        depends on NCLE_MQTT_ENABLE
        default ""
        help
            Username for brokers that require authentication (HiveMQ Cloud,
            the production server). Leave EMPTY for anonymous brokers such as
            the public test broker - the credentials are then not sent at all.

    config NCLE_MQTT_PASSWORD
        string "MQTT password"
        depends on NCLE_MQTT_ENABLE
        default ""
        help
            Password paired with NCLE_MQTT_USERNAME. Ignored when the username
            is empty. NOTE: this ends up in sdkconfig - do not commit a real
            production password to the repository.

    config NCLE_MQTT_RESTRICT_RISKY_CMDS
        bool "Block risky commands over MQTT (wifi_config/wifi_erase/reset_config)"
        depends on NCLE_MQTT_ENABLE
        default y
        help
            When enabled (default), wifi_config, wifi_erase and reset_config
            are REJECTED if received over MQTT (cloud) - they can cut the
            device off its network or wipe its setup, so they are allowed only
            over BLE / USB console (on-site). Disable to permit these remotely
            (e.g. for full remote management once the internal server is trusted).

    config NCLE_MQTT_STORE_FORWARD
        bool "Store-and-forward: buffer readings offline (LittleFS)"
        depends on NCLE_MQTT_ENABLE
        default y
        help
            When enabled (default), readings that occur while the broker is
            unreachable are saved to the `storage` flash partition (LittleFS)
            and flushed to the cloud on reconnect (oldest-first, deleted only
            after the broker ACKs). Survives power-off. When disabled, offline
            readings are dropped (BLE/console still deliver them).

endmenu
